# QA orchestration

For implementation and fix tasks, use this order. Do not skip a step.

1. Implement the smallest correct change.
2. Run targeted tests and record the real result.
3. Launch the `qa-reviewer` subagent (`.cursor/agents/qa-reviewer.md`) on the completed diff. It is read-only and independent.
4. Fix only findings the reviewer confirmed.
5. Re-run the targeted tests.
6. Launch `qa-reviewer` again on the updated diff.

Repeat steps 4–6 until the latest `qa-reviewer` verdict is **PASS**. A FAIL blocks completion, commit, push, and auto-merge. Do not weaken tests or product checks to obtain that PASS.

After PASS, follow the **Git policy** in `AGENTS.md`: commit, push the feature branch, open a non-draft pull request to `main`, and enable GitHub auto-merge only when branch protection and repository auto-merge are already enabled. Required GitHub Actions checks stay the merge authority. If those checks fail, fix the feature branch and push again. Never push to `main`, force-push, bypass protection, or use an admin override.

This rule does not replace `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, or the other Cursor rules. `main` stays protected.
